From e4996c3cf6812760696a0f73b53194f4a8b86c55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:28:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(post): initialize Sinumerik 810M cycle parameters and
 preserve spindle direction

Address the four safety review findings on PR #3317:
- Preserve active spindle direction (spinRev) through the section until endPreamble() so reverse L84 floating tapping sets R06=3 R07=4 and reverse L86 boring sets R07=4, without leaking into the next section.
- Initialize R11=3 (Z axis) before every L84 tapping call (both rigid R08=-3 and floating R08=-4) so L84 never inherits R11=1 from a preceding L83 DEEP cycle.
- Initialize L85 cutting and retraction feed parameters R16 and R17.
- Initialize L86 lateral retraction offsets R12=0 and R13=0.
- Add four pinning tests in crates/post/tests/sinumerik_810m_post.rs and regenerate the affected 810M tapping goldens (tap_plate.nc and synth_sinumerik-810m.nc).

Refs #2888
---
 assets/posts/sinumerik-810m.cps               |  10 +-
 .../golden/nc/sinumerik-810m/tap_plate.nc     |   2 +-
 .../tests/golden/nc/synth_sinumerik-810m.nc   |   2 +-
 crates/post/tests/sinumerik_810m_post.rs      | 246 +++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 249 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

